.TH CHTTP_REQUEST_GET_HEADER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_request_get_header \- look up a request header by name
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

const char *chttp_request_get_header(const chttp_request_t *req,
                                     const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the stored value for the named header, or NULL if no such
header exists.  The lookup is case-insensitive: the supplied name is
lowercased internally before the lookup is performed.

The returned pointer is valid until the next chttp_request_set_header
call on this request or until the request is freed.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
req   Request to query; may be NULL (returns NULL).
name  Header name; may be NULL (returns NULL).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Pointer to the stored value string, or NULL if not found.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_request_set_header (3)
